* @title Trace calls and returns of a recursive function
* @match substring/i
* @expect >>>
* LEVEL 0 RETURN OF FACT = 6
* <<<
* TRACE(name,'FUNCTION') asks the interpreter to announce every call and every
* return of a defined function, with the nesting depth in &FNCLEVEL. Running it
* over a recursive factorial prints the classic descend/ascend ladder:
*   LEVEL 0 CALL OF FACT(3) ... LEVEL 2 RETURN OF FACT = 1 ... and back up.
* We match the final top-level return, which only appears once the whole
* recursion has unwound correctly.
        DEFINE('FACT(N)')             :(MAIN)
FACT    FACT = LE(N,1) 1             :S(RETURN)
        FACT = N * FACT(N - 1)       :(RETURN)
MAIN    &TRACE = 100
        TRACE('FACT','FUNCTION')
        OUTPUT = FACT(3)
END
